<div class="static-page">
  <section class="static-page__intro">
    <h1>About Tempasi</h1>
    <p class="static-page__subtitle">
      A marketplace for exclusive website templates.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>What Tempasi is</h2>
    <p>
      Tempasi is a marketplace where designers sell and rent
      <strong>exclusive</strong> HTML/CSS/JS website templates. Once a
      template is bought or actively rented, it isn't available to anyone
      else for that period — you're not one of a thousand buyers of the
      same layout.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Buy or rent</h2>
    <p>
      Every template can be acquired two ways:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Buy</strong> — an outright purchase, the template is yours.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rent</strong> — a temporary exclusivity hold, so you can use
        the template for a client project without buying it outright. If you
        decide to buy later, the unused value of an active rental is
        converted into Tempasi credit and applied toward the purchase.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>
      Freelancers and agencies who need a polished template for a client
      project without committing to a full purchase, and designers who want
      to sell their work without it being resold to every visitor of a
      generic template store.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Reach out any time at
      <a href="mailto:support@tempasi.com">support@tempasi.com</a>.
      If you already have a Tempasi account, the
      <a href="/cabinet/support">Support</a> section in your cabinet has a
      short FAQ covering buying vs. renting, exclusivity, and credit.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
